lines=['# MG178 persistent-secondary tracker development results','',f"The new tracker carries possible second-core locations forward and lets the two cores move independently. It also estimates noise strength and time correlation from separate background references, with checks for species imbalance and persistent contamination. In fresh synthetic tests it passed {good}/{len(primary)} primary paths; the registered overall screen {'PASSED' if passed else 'FAILED'}. This tests the complete method beyond MG177’s known-primary diagnostic. All 24 original split controls were identified as multiple cores at their deadline. However, 13 primary paths were rejected by a noise guard that did not adequately handle uncertainty in estimated correlation, and acquisition/component failures remain. These are conditional engineering tests, not evidence of physical particle survival, and the method is not qualified to score the actual persistence trajectories.",'','## Frozen method','','Source/specification/input bindings and seed 17800 were published at `65ff1bb` before independent validation draws. Deterministic preflight passed four direct endpoint checks with primary and secondary moving in opposite directions. No Model G trajectories were generated. One worker, with one numerical-library thread; 2000-second evaluation cap, 400 MB full raw reserve.','', 'The primary retains stationary/moving modes. A surviving secondary has half its motion prior on exact stay and half uniformly over legal positions within two sites and one 0.125 width step, independently of the primary. New secondary births integrate the full 5655-position/width prior. Death and species-loss alternatives remain explicit structural transitions. Only the initial primary center is supplied; neither actual primary trajectories nor secondary coordinates are passed to the tracker.','', 'Geometry histories are compressed to eight endpoints per multiple/primary-mode pair, two for other nonabsent pairs and one for absent pairs, at most 30 states. Full pair masses are computed first and preserved during compression. This preserves probability mass but can discard useful geometry; it is not exact full-grid temporal inference. If no bounded secondary proposal is legal, the model resets its secondary prior uniformly and counts that operation. It is not a physical merger model.','', 'Each path has 16 independent spatial background fields for scalar noise strength and separate 64 time-ordered fields for GLS AR1 correlation estimation. Spatial and temporal references are independent of tracking data, and estimates remain fixed while tracking. The gate combines 8 frequency bands, channel balance, coherent mean, temporal innovation variance and correlation at lag two, with total nominal alpha 0.001 across 12 checks. Some reference distributions are approximate because rho is fitted. Likelihoods plug in estimated scale/rho; their uncertainty is not fully integrated, so weights remain approximate model weights. Known spectral shape, ordinary core amplitude and Gaussian/AR1 structure remain assumptions.','', '## Primary tests','','The original 264 paths span two noise regimes, two time correlations, three noise amplitudes and 11 cases, two paths/case. Acquisition requires two consecutive single labels ending by observation 5. Intact paths then need at least 90% single labels and 90% accurate single geometry after acquisition. Absence must never acquire; damaged and split controls must acquire by observation 5 and avoid a single label at 15. Reference rejection counts as failure rather than removing a path. Negative-control success can include uncertainty; it is not necessarily correct structural identification. These endpoints are retained from MG176, but different random fields and other method changes prevent attributing differences solely to secondary memory.','', '| Group | Successful / total |','|---|---:|',f"| Intact static/moving/deforming/stop–start | {sum(p['success'] for p in basepos)} / {len(basepos)} |",f"| Original negative controls | {sum(p['success'] for p in neg)} / {len(neg)} |",f"| Added secondary-motion/lifecycle tests | {sum(p['success'] for p in extra)} / {len(extra)} |",f"| Primary references adequate | {refs} / {len(primary)} |",'', '| Noise regime | Rho | Noise amplitude | Successful original paths / 22 |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
